# Rails web (`apps/web`)

## Rendering

- **SSR first** on `/artworks`: artwork tiles, result count, active facets, pagination in initial HTML
- Turbo Frame for facet changes, cart add, inline updates — not full page SPA navigation
- Stimulus for small DOM behaviour; Vue for rich widgets (mount into a div, props from data attributes)

## Controllers & views

- Thin controllers; query objects or model scopes for facet filtering
- Slim templates; partials for artwork tiles and facet chips
- Facet state driven by URL path segments, e.g. `/artworks/style/abstract/price/500-1000`

## Models

```ruby
# Facet scopes — chainable, URL-param driven
Artwork.by_style("abstract").by_price_range(500..1000).available
```

- `palette_data` jsonb on Artwork — do not compute palettes here; delegate to palette service
- Slugs for artists and artworks; indexed columns for facet filters

## Avoid

- Client-only listing pages with empty server HTML
- Fat models with colour math or image processing
- React/Vue for entire pages — islands only
